      "content": "Replaying on every subscription also replays on every route change: AppShell's subscription effect depends on `pathname`, and its callback sets `refusedAt` to the current path. After a foreign Restore, navigating to a record-entry URL therefore marks that newly visited path as the form that was open when replacement occurred, causing AppShell to render the entry form instead of `RecordEntryUnavailable`. Preserve replay for rebuilt shells, but distinguish replay from a fresh replacement (or adapt the consumer so replay cannot grant a new form-preservation exemption). Add an integration test for navigating to record entry after replacement.",
